-- title:
--   Stalk package at a supersingular point of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\neq 0$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$, and $K_1$ the one generated by the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$, with $K_1\le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and let $A$ act on $K$ and $K_1$ compatibly; let $j\in K$ and $j_1\in K_1$ be the elements whose Laurent expansions are the base-changed $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, both nonzero. Write $X$ and $\mathfrak Y$ for the two-chart integral models $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}$ over $A$ attached to $(K,j)$ and $(K_1,j_1)$, whose finite charts are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of the field integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j_1]$. Assume given: a morphism $m\colon X\to\mathfrak Y$; an $A$-algebra map $\iota_F$ of finite charts compatible with the embeddings into $L((q))$; compatibility of $m$ with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$; commutation of $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_F)$ and the finite-chart open immersions with $m$; equality of the $m$-preimage of the finite chart of $\mathfrak Y$ with the finite chart of $X$; finiteness of $m$ and of $\iota_F$; and the statement that an element of $K$ lies in the finite chart algebra exactly when it is integral over the image of $\iota_F$. Let $z\in X$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ via the structure morphism, assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and let $y$ be a point of the finite chart of $X$ mapping to $z$, such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ (with decidable equality) and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Then, with $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ the stalk map of $m$ regarded as an algebra structure, the following all hold: the same supersingularity statement for $j_1$ at the image of $y$ under $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_F)$; $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ is a finite $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}$-module and the stalk map is injective; both stalks have Krull dimension at least $2$; $\varpi_z\neq 0$; $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ is unramified over $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}$ at every non-maximal prime; every element of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ agrees modulo the maximal ideal with an element coming from $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}$; there exist algebra structures making $K_1$ a fraction field of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}$ and $\mathrm{extendScalars}\,hle$ (the field $K$ viewed as a $K_1$-extension) a fraction field of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, with the two evident scalar towers; and, for every $\varpi$-adically complete discrete valuation domain $W$ with a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $\sigma\varpi$, if the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak Y,m(z)}$ is ring-isomorphic to the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ modulo the crossing ideal at $(\sigma\varpi)^{p-1}$, then $p-1$ is a unit in $W$ and $W$ contains a primitive $(p-1)$-st root of unity.
--
--   This is the packaging statement that converts the chart-level information about the stable two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$ — finiteness and total ramification of the map to the $\Gamma_0(p)$-floor model at a supersingular point, unramifiedness away from the closed point, the dimension count, and the coefficient facts — into the stalk-level data consumed downstream. It is used by the statement identifying the completed local ring at such a point with a crossing model and deducing the tame local structure.
